tvm-ffi provides CMake targets:

    find_package(tvm_ffi CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE tvm_ffi::tvm_ffi)

The target selects the installed static or shared runtime. Static linkage requires
CMake 3.24 or newer and retains all built-in function registrations automatically.
When linking the static archive directly, use the linker's whole-archive option
(for example, /WHOLEARCHIVE:tvm_ffi_static.lib on MSVC) and link the platform
dependencies (DbgHelp on Windows; threads and dl where required on Unix).

Use the shared runtime when multiple DLLs/modules need to share a single function
and type registry. Statically linking the runtime into each module creates
separate registries.
